KG42.register("clusters-4c93c8586a928b7572ba9f1e",{"id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v142-d-K002","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","label":"Price-quantity bidding and iterative adjustment with non-decreasing utility","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K002","label":"Price-quantity bidding and iterative adjustment with non-decreasing utility","market_meaning":"Participating players form price-quantity bids based on external trading prices, previous-round transaction results, and their own optimization results, and adjust them under the requirement that utility does not decrease. HSSA generates electricity supply and demand bids after a preliminary clearing without its own participation; its increase-supply or reduce-demand response remains optional.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","participation"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"DG electricity supply, Load electricity use, HV hydrogen use, and HSSA electricity supply and demand respectively apply the original-chain conditions. The previous-round electricity price and the current-round price without HSSA are different inputs; the fact that HSSA supply and demand bids share a price benchmark does not mean that positive supply and demand quantities must be submitted simultaneously. The participation Rule-Chain provides only the corresponding roles and previous-round price conditions.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Supply and demand bids are described by the same source as being updated based on clearing feedback and own utility, and form complementary decisions through the HSSA common price benchmark and the optional increase-supply and reduce-demand responses. Clearing optimization and result publication belong to the next Rule-Cluster; this Rule-Cluster retains the bid-function boundary and the explicit gap in update closure.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries demand price-quantity formation, Load price adjustment, and the optional HSSA reduce-demand response."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries supply price-quantity formation, clearing feedback, and the optional HSSA increase-supply response."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Only references the Load previous-round participation condition and the buyer role, and does not count them again as a new participation rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Only references the DG previous-round participation condition and the HSSA bidding participation mode and preliminary-clearing timing."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-lambda-L-prev","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-lambda-DS"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C012"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g02-e12"],"rationale":"The price comparison for Load's previous-round participation and the next-round segmented bid use the same previous-round electricity price and DisCo selling price; the distinct roles of the participation condition and the bid function are retained, and no sufficient participation criterion for the current round is inferred."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C008","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C009"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e16"],"rationale":"The DG previous-round price condition defines its bidding context, and the HSSA preliminary-clearing timing provides the price source for the supply bid; the two types of conditions apply separately and do not substitute for each other."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g03-e001"],"rationale":"HSSA's bidding participation mode as an electricity buyer is specified by the demand-bid condition; its pricing benchmark comes from the same-round preliminary clearing without HSSA."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R001::theta::theta_lambda_LnA"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C009","v141-c-R002::theta::theta_lnA_price"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e16"],"rationale":"HSSA's demand and supply bids use the same preliminary clearing price, but each retains a different quantity upper bound and applicable conditions; the two bid price decisions are not merged into the same object."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e23"],"rationale":"The two Rule-Chains record HSSA's optional increase-supply or reduce-demand response under the same supply-shortage and price-rise situation; these are complementary responses under the same conditions and do not mean that both must occur or are causally related."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::x_dg_offer_qty","v141-c-R002::x::x_hssa_offer_qty"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::theta_DG_offer","v141-c-R001::theta::theta_HSSA_offer","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e21"],"rationale":"The same-round declared supply quantity serves as an input for total-supply comparison in Load's price-adjustment judgment; the supplier's decision and the demand side's observation parameter retain different local roles."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O01","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::theta_lambda_L_prev","v141-c-R002::theta::theta_prev_lem_price","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-lambda-L-prev","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_lambda_L_prev"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g02-e12"],"rationale":"Under the same time slot and previous-round index, both refer to the already-formed LEM electricity price; the bidding benchmark and the two types of participation checks still retain their respective parameter roles."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O02","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::theta_lambda_DS","v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-lambda-DS"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g02-e12"],"rationale":"Both are the DisCo selling price for the same time slot, used respectively for the Load bid and participation comparison, and their local input objects are not merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::theta_disco_purchase_price","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_lambda_DP"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13"],"rationale":"Both are the DisCo purchase price paid to DG, serving respectively as the supply bid and the previous-round participation comparison."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::theta_lambda_LnA","v141-c-R002::theta::theta_lnA_price"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e16"],"rationale":"Both refer to the same-round preliminary clearing price without HSSA, but they respectively serve HSSA's demand and supply bids and are not rewritten as a common parameter."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::x_dg_offer_qty","v141-c-R001::theta::theta_DG_offer"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g02-e21"],"rationale":"When the indices are aligned, they are the same DG current-round supply quantity; the former is the supply decision, and the latter is the observation input for Load's price-adjustment judgment."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::x_hssa_offer_qty","v141-c-R001::theta::theta_HSSA_offer"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e21"],"rationale":"When the indices are aligned, they are the same HSSA current-round declared supply quantity, retaining the distinction between the decision variable and the price-adjustment judgment parameter."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-O07","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R002::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R007::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g02-e14"],"rationale":"The same frozen node can be displayed uniformly; this display mapping is not equivalent to external prices, previous-round prices, current-round preliminary prices, or the prices of the two energy carriers."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"All new connections in this Rule-Cluster use only candidate evidence permitted by the experiment; B remains unreviewed, and the bid transcription and mathematical interpretation have no independent source-review conclusion.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C008","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C009"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e23"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check item by item the segment intervals, iteration indices, optional responses, and corresponding sources, and retain the frozen C objects until explicit revision."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The adjacent intervals in Eqs. (32)-(34) are all closed intervals, and the common endpoint can simultaneously trigger both bids; the previous-round participation conditions for DG and Load also allow the two bids to be explicitly different, and HV likewise does not provide an endpoint-selection convention. The current chains are insufficient to constitute a single-valued bid function.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C012","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C013","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C008","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e13"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the original equations and have C clarify the applicable convention for the common endpoint or retain its ambiguity; D does not arbitrarily change the open/closed intervals or select one of the prices."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G03","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The bid evidence uses N_s, but it does not explicitly give a general definition, nor whether DG, Load, and HV use the same scenario set. R001 interprets it as the number of scenarios, whereas R002 leaves the definition unspecified; they cannot be merged merely because the symbols are the same, and a case scenario count cannot be entered into the general rule.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::theta_N_s","v141-c-R002::theta::theta_N_s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e26"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the scenario count, the sample set, and the relationship between the mean and the scenario weights, and then have C make the definitions and the cross-chain correspondence explicit; also clarify the index discrepancy between tth iteration in the original text of equation (32) and r in the formula."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G04","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The evidence contains equations (45)-(46) for DG raising its bid, and the correction steps by which DG and Load correct an ineffective adjustment from the previous round; R002 retains only the general feedback and utility requirements and has no corresponding DG-conditional update, while the correction constraint in R001 covers only Load.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C006","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C011"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e21"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"C is to explicitly record the DG update conditions and correction scope already given by the source, and bind the existing variables; this round does not directly supply the missing constraint from the supply-demand symmetry narrative."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G05","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The bid function depends on the previous round's price and transaction quantity. The source states the first-round external utility benchmark and the initial zero accepted quantity, but the frozen chain has not formed a citable complete initialization condition, so the subsequent-round function cannot automatically be treated as the first-round procedure.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::theta_load_deal_prev","v141-c-R001::theta::theta_HV_LEM_purchase_prev","v141-c-R002::theta::theta_prev_dg_deal","v141-c-R001::theta::theta_lambda_L_prev","v141-c-R002::theta::theta_prev_lem_price"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e10","v141-b-g02-e16"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"C is to distinguish first-round initialization from subsequent-round updates, and make explicit the initial values and external trading benchmarks, for each role, that already have source support; the HV initialization that has not been stated continues to be retained as a gap."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G06","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Being higher than the external-trading utility, an adjustment not reducing utility, and correcting the previous round's adjustment are all procedural requirements; the current bidding chain has no closed mathematical interface for utility comparison, cross-period strategy evaluation, and the correction quantity.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C009","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C010","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C011","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E07","v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e25"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"C is to make explicit the inputs and outputs of local utility optimization and bid adjustment, and the evaluation period; a correction algorithm or step size may be added only with source support, and case parameters cannot substitute for the general update rule."}]},"rule_refs":["47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R007","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R008"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-272a6ce8ab154b93","COMP-6786c966fc7c0aa0","COMP-b1b0c5e3c8ca187b","COMP-c19b72437a1d5a78","COMP-c8696bb2d6d47f04","COMP-e7c615345112f85e"]});
